{"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM"]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizedTensor","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizedLayoutMetadata","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizedLinear","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizationScheme","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalQuantizedEngine","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalQuantizedError"],"title":"Quantization & Metal Execution","anchor":"Quantization--Metal-Execution"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Large language models like Llama 3, Mistral, and DeepSeek require massive memory bandwidth. Weight-only quantization (such as GGUF Q4_0 and Q8_0) compresses 16-bit floating-point weights into 4-bit or 8-bit integer blocks with group scaling factors, reducing memory footprint by 50% to 75%.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"SwiftLLM","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" implements native Metal Shading Language (MSL) SIMD kernels executing hardware dequantization and GEMV \/ GEMM transformations directly on Apple Silicon GPUs without intermediate CPU memory allocations.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"Architecture","type":"heading","anchor":"Architecture"},{"code":["Packed Quantized Weights [Q4_0 \/ Q8_0]   Scale Factors [FP16]   Input Activations [FP32]","                 │                               │                        │","                 └───────────────────────┬───────┴────────────────────────┘","                                         ▼","                   Metal Compute Command Encoder","                                         │","                 ┌───────────────────────┴───────────────────────┐","                 ▼                                               ▼","     MSL Kernel: gemv_q4_0                           MSL Kernel: gemv_q8_0","   - Unpack 4-bit nibbles (w - 8)                  - Load signed 8-bit integers","   - Multiply by group FP16 scale                  - Multiply by group FP16 scale","   - Accumulate with input vector                  - Accumulate with input vector","                 │                                               │","                 └───────────────────────┬───────────────────────┘","                                         ▼","                            Output Activation Vector","                               (Unified Memory)"],"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"SIMD-Group Matrix Multiplication","type":"heading","anchor":"SIMD-Group-Matrix-Multiplication"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"On Apple Silicon (M-series GPUs), threads within a 32-thread SIMD-group collaborate on 8x8 matrix tiles using "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"metal_simdgroup_matrix"},{"type":"text","text":". This eliminates thread divergence and ensures maximal utilization of the GPU arithmetic units:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["#include <metal_stdlib>","#include <metal_simdgroup_matrix>","","using namespace metal;","","kernel void gemm_simdgroup_q4_0(","    device const half* A               [[buffer(0)]],","    device const half* B               [[buffer(1)]],","    device half* C                     [[buffer(2)]],","    constant uint& M                   [[buffer(3)]],","    constant uint& N                   [[buffer(4)]],","    constant uint& K                   [[buffer(5)]],","    uint2 threadgroup_position_in_grid [[threadgroup_position_in_grid]],","    uint simdgroup_index_in_threadgroup [[simdgroup_index_in_threadgroup]]",") {","    simdgroup_matrix<half, 8, 8> acc;","    acc = make_filled_simdgroup_matrix<half, 8, 8>(0.0h);","    \/\/ Accumulate across inner K dimension...","}"],"syntax":"metal","type":"codeListing"},{"level":2,"text":"Swift API Integration: From QuantizedTensor to Metal GEMV","type":"heading","anchor":"Swift-API-Integration-From-QuantizedTensor-to-Metal-GEMV"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiftLLM"},{"type":"text","text":" unifies parsed weight storage and GPU execution through a zero-copy pipeline:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"$$\\text{GGUF File} \\xrightarrow{\\text{GGUFParser}} \\text{QuantizedTensor} \\xrightarrow{\\text{extractSeparatedBuffers}} \\text{QuantizedLinear.forwardMetal} \\xrightarrow{\\text{MSL SIMD}} \\text{Output Activation}$$"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"1. Extracting Separated Buffers from QuantizedTensor","type":"heading","anchor":"1-Extracting-Separated-Buffers-from-QuantizedTensor"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"QuantizedTensor"},{"type":"text","text":" preserves the raw binary layout (e.g. 18-byte Q4_0 blocks) with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"QuantizedLayoutMetadata"},{"type":"text","text":", allowing separation of packed weights and scale factors:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["import Foundation","import SwiftLLM","","\/\/ 1. Load tensor from parsed GGUF dictionary","guard let tensor = parsedWeights[\"blk.0.attn_q.weight\"],","      let buffers = tensor.extractSeparatedBuffers() else {","    fatalError(\"Failed to extract quantized buffers\")","}","","let packedWeights: Data = buffers.weights","let packedScales: Data = buffers.scales"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"2. Direct Metal Kernel Execution via QuantizedLinear","type":"heading","anchor":"2-Direct-Metal-Kernel-Execution-via-QuantizedLinear"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"QuantizedLinear"},{"type":"text","text":" encapsulates both MLX-accelerated layer evaluations and native Metal MSL shader execution ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gemv_q4_0"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"gemv_q8_0"},{"type":"text","text":"):"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["\/\/ 2. Initialize layer geometry and scheme","let linear = QuantizedLinear(","    inFeatures: 4096,","    outFeatures: 4096,","    scheme: .q4_0,","    weight: tensor.dequantizeToFloat(), \/\/ MLXArray fallback\/graph evaluation","    scales: MLXArray(0.0)",")","","\/\/ 3. Direct Metal GEMV execution without CPU round-trips or allocations","let outputActivations: [Float] = try linear.forwardMetal(","    inVector: inputActivations,","    rawWeights: packedWeights,","    rawScalesData: packedScales",")"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalShadersQuantization","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"Hardware dequantization and SIMD-group matrix multiplication for 4-bit and 8-bit quantized weights on Apple Silicon GPU.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/TransformerDecoderArchitecture","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/TransformerDecoderInference","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/SamplingAndDecodingStrategies","doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/WeightParsingAndSampling"],"generated":true,"title":"Guides & Tutorials","anchor":"Guides--Tutorials"}],"metadata":{"title":"Native Metal MSL Shaders for Quantized LLMs","modules":[{"name":"SwiftLLM"}],"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftllm\/metalshadersquantization"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Local Causal Transformer Decoder & Weight Parsers.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm","kind":"symbol","title":"SwiftLLM"},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/SamplingAndDecodingStrategies":{"abstract":[{"text":"Control autoregressive language generation with Temperature, Top-P Nucleus, Top-K, and Repetition Penalty.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/SamplingAndDecodingStrategies","kind":"article","title":"Token Sampling & Decoding Strategies","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/samplinganddecodingstrategies","role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/WeightParsingAndSampling":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/WeightParsingAndSampling","type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"GGUF\/SafeTensors Parsing & Sampling","url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/weightparsingandsampling","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Parse GGUF and SafeTensors model weights zero-copy into Apple Silicon unified memory and sample tokens with fine-grained logits controls."}],"role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/QuantizedLinear":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/quantizedlinear","role":"symbol","type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"QuantizedLinear","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"QuantizedLinear","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A linear neural network layer performing matrix multiplication with 4-bit (Q4_0, Q4_K) or 8-bit quantized weights.","type":"text"}],"title":"QuantizedLinear","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizedLinear"},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/TransformerDecoderInference":{"url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/transformerdecoderinference","role":"collectionGroup","type":"topic","kind":"article","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Execute two-stage autoregressive generation with full prompt prefill and incremental single-token decoding using Apple Silicon KV-caching."}],"title":"Autoregressive Transformer Decoder Inference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/TransformerDecoderInference"},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/QuantizedTensor":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A semantic representation of a parsed tensor preserving raw quantized layout without eager dequantization."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizedTensor","type":"topic","title":"QuantizedTensor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"QuantizedTensor"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"QuantizedTensor"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/quantizedtensor"},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/TransformerDecoderArchitecture":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/TransformerDecoderArchitecture","type":"topic","title":"Transformer Architecture & LLM Inference Guide","kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/transformerdecoderarchitecture","abstract":[{"text":"High-throughput, on-device causal language model execution on Apple Silicon Unified Memory Architecture using ","type":"text"},{"code":"TransformerDecoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"PagedKVCache","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"GGUFParser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and ","type":"text"},{"code":"SafeTensorsParser","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"role":"article"},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/QuantizedLayoutMetadata":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"QuantizedLayoutMetadata"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Scheme-specific layout metadata for quantized tensors.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizedLayoutMetadata","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"QuantizedLayoutMetadata"}],"title":"QuantizedLayoutMetadata","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/quantizedlayoutmetadata","role":"symbol"},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/QuantizationScheme":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/QuantizationScheme","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"QuantizationScheme","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"QuantizationScheme","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"QuantizationScheme","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/quantizationscheme","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The quantization scheme used for compressed model weights."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/MetalQuantizedEngine":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A thread-safe executor and pipeline cache for Metal quantized MSL GEMV \/ GEMM kernels."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalQuantizedEngine","title":"MetalQuantizedEngine","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MetalQuantizedEngine","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MetalQuantizedEngine","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/metalquantizedengine"},"doc://SwiftLLM/documentation/SwiftLLM/MetalQuantizedError":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MetalQuantizedError","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"MetalQuantizedError","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MetalQuantizedError"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Errors occurring during Metal quantized kernel pipeline creation or GPU buffer execution."}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swiftllm\/metalquantizederror","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftLLM\/documentation\/SwiftLLM\/MetalQuantizedError","role":"symbol"}}}